# GroupPlacement suite (plan wb079-unified-77f68967, Task 11 / C4+C5).
# The fixture includes production_core_host.cpp and editor.cpp exactly once. This permits native NPC
# packet-boundary setup without a new production seam. All queue/registry/editor behavior stays real.
# production_core_host.cpp compiles the actual production core TU once with WB_UNIFIED_HOST_TEST (the engine
# boundaries route through host::Seam(); the registry, the queues, the pump dispatch, the group admission
# (AdmitGroupCopy), the C4 copy-envelope provenance and the C5 per-record rows stay production code). The
# fixture textually includes the actual editor.cpp once, so the camera-aware grab (StartGrab/Place/Member),
# DropCarried/CancelCarried and the History under test are the shipped ones. The shipped proj_codec.cpp and
# wb_group_math.cpp are linked as their own TUs (the same ones build.bat compiles). The real input.cpp and Win32
# backend are linked (INPUT); only the service boundaries CORE does not link (thumbgen, httpapi, overlay
# textures, MinHook) are explicit host substitutes in production_core_host.cpp.
@include tools/imgui
@include tools/imgui/backends
@include tools/minhook/include
@define WB_UNIFIED_HOST_TEST
@define _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS
asi/cdmodkit/overlay_discovery.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/report_projection.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/proj_codec.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/wb_group_math.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/i18n.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/icons.cpp
asi/cdmodkit/input.cpp
# v0.95 adaptation (WB080 Task 2 repair B1): the shipped environment.cpp provides
